Hyrax homomorphic batching — four scenarios
Date: 2026-11-10
STATUS: ALL FOUR COMPLETED; independent hidden-evaluation verification passed.
Implementation: local poly-commit Hyrax snapshot, BN254, Merlin transcript; native commit/open/check unchanged.
Batching: commit each original matrix, derive coefficients after all commitments, aggregate matrices, blinding factors and commitments by equal padded size.
CPU only; 48 prover threads, sequential independent verifier; each scenario once.
Timing: prover = commit + aggregation + native opening/serialization. Input conversion, field loading and parameter setup excluded.
Verifier includes file reads, proof decoding, transcript derivation and original commitment aggregation; setup/metadata parsing excluded.
Proof size sums the five group proofs; original commitments and public metadata are separate.
Native check validates hidden evaluation commitments; supplied public values are ignored. This is not public-evaluation checking.
Native setup is testing-only; these are implementation benchmarks, not a production-security claim.

